@.str.155 = private unnamed_addr constant [966 x i8] c"Compute the convex hull of a triangle mesh using qhull. This runs on the CPU.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    joggle_inputs (default False): Handle precision problems by randomly perturbing the input data. Set to True if perturbing the input is acceptable but you need convex simplicial output. If False, neighboring facets may be merged in case of precision problems. See `QHull docs <http://www.qhull.org/html/qh-impre.htm#joggle>`__ for more details.\0A\0AReturn:\0A    TriangleMesh representing the convexh hull. This contains an\0A    extra vertex property `point_indices` that contains the index of the\0A    corresponding vertex in the original mesh.\0A\0AExample:\0A    We will load the Eagle dataset, compute and display it's convex hull::\0A\0A        eagle = o3d.data.EaglePointCloud()\0A        pcd = o3d.t.io.read_point_cloud(eagle.path)\0A        hull = pcd.compute_convex_hull()\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([{'name': 'eagle', 'geometry': pcd}, {'name': 'convex hull', 'geometry': hull}])\0A    \00", align 1
