@.str.192 = private unnamed_addr constant [761 x i8] c"Sweeps the point set rotationally about an axis.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    angle (float): The rotation angle in degree.\0A\0A    axis (open3d.core.Tensor): The rotation axis.\0A\0A    resolution (int): The resolution defines the number of intermediate sweeps\0A        about the rotation axis.\0A\0A    translation (float): The translation along the rotation axis.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A line set with the result of the sweep operation.\0A\0A\0AExample:\0A\0A    This code generates a number of helices from a point cloud::\0A\0A        import open3d as o3d\0A        import numpy as np\0A        pcd = o3d.t.geometry.PointCloud(np.random.rand(10,3))\0A        helices = pcd.extrude_rotation(3*360, [0,1,0], resolution=3*16, translation=2)\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([{'name': 'helices', 'geometry': helices}])\0A\0A\00", align 1
